                <pb facs="1057" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg958"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3131/66: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Villard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-05T15:00:00-05:00">December 5, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Your 82 is receiving consideration and instructions will be sent you in a few
                    days.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph whether there is likelihood of obtaining substantial concessions
                    without some concession by the U. S. on petroleum.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
